/-
# Squares of products modulo fourth powers in free products (Kourovka Notebook Problem 3.8)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 3.8 (V. G. Vilyatser): let `G` be the free
product of free groups `A` and `B`, and `V` the verbal subgroup of `G` corresponding to the equation
`x⁴ = 1`. Is it true that, if `a ∈ A \ V` and `b ∈ B \ V`, then `(ab)² ∉ V`?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.Coprod.Basic
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.FreeGroup.Basic

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.FreeProductFourthPowersKourovka3Problem8Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 3.8 (V. G.
Vilyatser). UnsolvedMath record UM-00700162 (`KOU-3.8`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

`A = F(α)` and `B = F(β)` are free groups on arbitrary sets of generators and `G` is Mathlib's free
product `Monoid.Coprod A B`, with `A`, `B` embedded by `inl`, `inr`. The verbal subgroup for `x⁴ =
1` is the subgroup generated by all fourth powers. The refutation is one explicit pair of words
whose verification rests on Wright's results on groups of exponent four, not on a decision procedure
on a finite object.
-/

/-- The verbal subgroup of `G` for the law `x⁴ = 1`: the subgroup generated by all fourth
powers. -/
def fourthPowerSubgroup (G : Type*) [Group G] : Subgroup G :=
  Subgroup.closure {g | ∃ h : G, g = h ^ 4}

/-- Kourovka 3.8 (V. G. Vilyatser): let `G = A * B` be the free product of free groups `A` and `B`
and `V` the verbal subgroup of `G` for `x⁴ = 1`. If `a ∈ A \ V` and `b ∈ B \ V`, then
`(ab)² ∉ V`. -/
def squareOfProductAvoidsFourthPowers : Prop :=
  ∀ (α β : Type) (a : FreeGroup α) (b : FreeGroup β),
    Monoid.Coprod.inl a ∉ fourthPowerSubgroup (Monoid.Coprod (FreeGroup α) (FreeGroup β)) →
    Monoid.Coprod.inr b ∉ fourthPowerSubgroup (Monoid.Coprod (FreeGroup α) (FreeGroup β)) →
    (Monoid.Coprod.inl a * Monoid.Coprod.inr b) ^ 2 ∉
      fourthPowerSubgroup (Monoid.Coprod (FreeGroup α) (FreeGroup β))

/--
Resolved false: the Kourovka Archive answers 3.8 "No, it is not": in the free product of two free
groups of rank `2` with bases `a₁, a₂` and `b₁, b₂`, the commutators `a = [[a₁, a₂, a₂], [a₁, a₂]]`
and `b = [[b₁, b₂, b₂], [b₁, b₂]]` lie outside `V` while `(ab)² ∈ V`, because `a²`, `b²` and `[a,
b]` lie in `V` by Wright's results on groups of exponent four (Roman'kov 1970). Source: E. I.
Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st
issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 3.8 (V. G. Vilyatser);
resolution: V. A. Roman'kov, talk at the seminar Algebra and Logic, 17 March 1970 (counterexample
recorded in the Kourovka Archive); C. R. B. Wright, On the nilpotency class of a group of exponent
four, Pacific J. Math. 11 (1961), 387-394, Archive text: for free groups `A`, `B` with bases `a₁,
a₂` and `b₁, b₂`, the commutators `a = [[a₁, a₂, a₂], [a₁, a₂]]` and `b = [[b₁, b₂, b₂], [b₁, b₂]]`
do not belong to `V` but `(ab)² ∈ V`, since `a² ∈ V`, `b² ∈ V` and `[a, b] ∈ V` by Wright's paper;
Kourovka Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 3.8: No, it is not,
https://doi.org/10.2140/pjm.1961.11.387.
-/
public theorem_wanted squareOfProductAvoidsFourthPowers_refuted :
    ¬ squareOfProductAvoidsFourthPowers

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.FreeProductFourthPowersKourovka3Problem8Wanted
